text/html; charset=utf-8,f82f97b38d39a18c7a913c7c241024e107c0d18c6d2664fbe3589841b3ebfb3e,retained prior type,0,"DFR Report HTML --> --> --> IPEDS DATA FEEDBACK REPORT 2022 --> What Is IPEDS? The Integrated Postsecondary Education Data System (IPEDS) is a system of survey components that collects data from all institutions that provide postsecondary education and are eligible to receive Title IV funding across the United States and other U.S. jurisdictions. These data are used at the federal and state level for policy analysis and development; at the institutional level for benchmarking and peer analysis; and by students and parents, through the College Navigator ( https://nces.ed.gov/collegenavigator/ )","{""bounded_link_count"": 45, ""bounded_visible_character_count"": 43974, ""html_title"": ""DFR Report HTML""}",127420,https://nces.ed.gov/ipeds/dfr/2022/ReportHTML.aspx?unitId=260336,EXTLOC-177c386025d7afb3529fd283,,non_safety|police,html,200,staffing_table,https://nces.ed.gov/ipeds/dfr/2022/ReportHTML.aspx?unitId=260336,high,0,0,False,EXTCAND-7d697fae002064a5ab41d8d5,,MECHEXP-331bac4d38a14970e8f45075|MECHEXP-71c605ed14f3b21dc0af020b|MECHEXP-731a3079cfa11aebc502a608|MECHEXP-8e6631676f61bb1f1fcf8c32|MECHEXP-c6c68b47b29ef27d3f484c04|MECHEXP-d00939d0b6dbb7597091d6e3|MECHEXP-e42781d6aa5f13fc14bae031|MECHEXP-eca366bf9c4f3b085f6abe05|MECHEXP-f5e9a12b6d64e10f1b9be16e,ROOTCOMP-25d3f36d31b1196f9e1ab976|ROOTCOMP-814abcde6fd950476c7ab9d3,external_search_wave_001_compacted,artifacts/local_retained_sources/whole_corpus_external_data_exhaustive_pipeline_2026-08-04/html/f82f97b38d39a18c7a913c7c241024e107c0d18c6d2664fbe3589841b3ebfb3e.html,nces.ed.gov,Jackson,0,true,ReportHTML.aspx,2021,multi_family_administrative_source,staffing_table,html_text_candidate,1,EXTSOURCE-e2513264acee78ba148583f3,2026-08-05T17:25:44.528328+00:00,0,implementation_confirmation|recruitment_and_retention|staffing_and_headcount|tenure_and_progression,non_safety|police,official_administrative_summary,EXTSRC